# New Feature Considerations

When adding new features to the codebase, you must ensure proper integration with existing systems. This document outlines the systems that must be updated when adding different types of features.

## Discord Embed System

**When**: Adding any feature that displays user-generated or variable-length content in Discord embeds.

**Required Actions**:
- **Always** use `addLongField()` from `src/app/bot/utils/embed-helpers.ts` for potentially long text
- **Never** directly call `embed.addFields()` with content that could exceed 1024 characters
- Discord embed field values have a hard limit of 1024 characters; exceeding this causes runtime validation errors

**Example:**
```typescript
import { addLongField } from "../../utils/embed-helpers.js";

// ✅ Correct - handles long content automatically
addLongField(embed, "📦 Items", itemList);

// ❌ Wrong - will crash if itemList exceeds 1024 chars
embed.addFields({ name: "📦 Items", value: itemList });
```

**Applies to**: Commands displaying lists, inventories, generated content, or any variable-length content in embed fields.

